4.2 Architectural Options, Trade-Offs & Recommendation
The Master Specification (§5.13, §6.3, §9.3, §11.4) mandates strict financial-like invariants: no negative Spendable XP, atomic mission escrow/refunds, duplicate payout/scoring prevention under concurrency, and strict referential integrity across 28 entities.
Architectural Dimension	Option A (Recommended)	Option B	Option C
Backend + Database	Node/Express (server.ts integrated with Vite) + Hosted PostgreSQL (e.g., AI Studio Cloud SQL) using a typed SQL schema/ORM (e.g., Drizzle or Prisma).	Managed BaaS / NoSQL (e.g., Firebase Auth + Firestore) with Cloud Functions / server transactions.	Separated Serverless API + Managed Postgres (e.g., Supabase / Neon + external API).
Trade-offs	Pros: Native ACID transactions (SELECT ... FOR UPDATE), relational foreign keys across 28 entities, SQL SUM reconciliation for XP/CP ledgers, seasonal leaderboard window queries, runs cleanly on port 3000 via server.ts in AI Studio.
Cons: Requires managing DB schema migrations and provisioning Postgres.	Pros: Fast auth bootstrap and realtime listeners.
Cons: Multi-document escrow/refund/CP-cap invariants, relational joins across Houses/Permissions/Leaderboards, and strict private-evidence ACLs are harder to model and audit cleanly in NoSQL than in relational SQL; adds vendor lock-in.	Pros: Built-in Auth/Storage/Postgres bundle.
Cons: Introduces external platform credentials and split deployment surface outside the single AI Studio runtime.
Auth & Sessions	HTTP-only secure session cookies backed by server sessions table (or verified Firebase/OIDC tokens exchanged for server session), email verification + password reset via email provider.	Managed client SDK token passed via Authorization: Bearer to backend API.	Magic-link / OAuth-only without local passwords.
Evidence Storage	External Object Storage (S3/GCS signed upload URLs) with server-side MIME/size/ownership validation & private-by-default download proxying (MVP fallback: validated URL/metadata + capped private upload store).	Database bytea/blobs (simple initially, degrades DB size/backups).	External links only (simplest, weakest proof preservation on disputes).
Recommendation (PROPOSED, awaiting human approval): Adopt Option A (server.ts Express API + Managed PostgreSQL + HTTP-only server sessions + Signed Object Storage) because it aligns directly with AI Studio's single-server runtime (port 3000), provides strict ACID guarantees for XP escrow and settlement without client trust, cleanly supports all 28 relational entities in Spec §6.1, and keeps vitest/API integration testing deterministic.
