8. Outstanding Technical & Governance Decisions
All 30 level thresholds, 5 Ascendancy ranks + Spartan identity, 12 system XP values, 4 mission reward bands, 14 CP values + seasonal caps, 5 leaderboard categories, and 19 achievements are already established as configurable BASELINE values in Spec v1.0 and are NOT open blockers.
Only genuine unresolved decisions (aligned with Spec §16 and system architecture choices) remain for stakeholder/human approval:
Technical Provider Decisions (Required Before Phase 1)
Final Database & Backend API Architecture: Approve Option A (server.ts Express API + Managed PostgreSQL, e.g., AI Studio Cloud SQL) vs. Option B (Firebase/Firestore) vs. Option C (External BaaS).
Production Authentication & Connected-Account Strategy: Confirm session mechanism (HTTP-only session cookies vs. managed auth tokens), password reset email provider, and whether Web3 wallet / social linking in Settings is connect-only identity metadata in v1.0.
File & Evidence Storage Provider + Retention Rules: Confirm object storage provider (e.g., GCS/S3 signed uploads vs. URL-only at initial launch), file size/MIME caps, and evidence-retention windows (Spec §16).
Operational & Governance Rules (Spec §16 — Required Before Phases 4–6)
Ascendancy Appointment Authority: Exact authority matrix for appointing Vanguard, Gladiator, Strategos, Elder, and Champion.
Reviewer Appointment, Replacement & Multi-Allocation Rules: Rules for assigning/replacing non-creator reviewers (Elder/Strategos/designated) and handling multi-contributor mission budget splits / partial completion payouts.
Pre-Publication Mission Moderation Scope: Which mission categories or reward tiers (in addition to >Major >1,500 XP) require mandatory pre-publication moderation before going Published/Active.
Organisation Verification Workflow: Minimum checks required for any Spartan-created Organisation profile (ACC-002) to gain verified sponsor badge or sponsor-funded mission privileges.
Notification Delivery Channels & Preferences: Confirm in-app notifications only for v1.0 vs. email/digest channels.
Final Academy Content Catalogue: Curated lesson/module/path content and practical assessment rubrics to seed AcademyContent (Spec §2.2 explicitly instructs not to invent the operational content catalogue).
Final Administrative Permission Matrix: Fine-grained permission defaults across House manager, Mentor, Event manager, Content manager, Moderator, Finance administrator, and Platform administrator.
